cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Eulerian Video Magnification, on processors and any graphics hardware"
message: >-
  If you use this software in work you publish, please cite both this
  implementation and the original method it implements.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kucuk
    given-names: Furkan
repository-code: "https://github.com/iamkucuk/eulerian-video-magnification-cuda"
url: "https://iamkucuk.github.io/eulerian-video-magnification-cuda/"
abstract: >-
  An implementation of Eulerian Video Magnification that amplifies colour and
  motion changes in video too small to see, together with the phase-based
  follow-up method. Includes a NumPy implementation checked against the original
  authors' published output, a hand-written CUDA version for NVIDIA hardware,
  and three portable versions — OpenCL, Apple's Metal, and Vulkan — that reach
  Apple, AMD and Intel hardware and any future device with a standard driver.
  Every version is compared against the NumPy reference by an automated test
  suite.
keywords:
  - eulerian video magnification
  - motion magnification
  - video processing
  - computer vision
